{
  "sn12.24:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.24 ",
  "sn12.24:0.2": "3. The Ten Powers ",
  "sn12.24:0.3": "Followers of Other Religions ",
  "sn12.24:1.1": "Near Rājagaha, in the Bamboo Grove. ",
  "sn12.24:1.2": "Then Venerable Sāriputta robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Rājagaha for alms. ",
  "sn12.24:1.3": "Then it occurred to him, ",
  "sn12.24:1.4": "“It’s too early to wander for alms in Rājagaha. ",
  "sn12.24:1.5": "Why don’t I visit the monastery for the wanderers of other religions?” ",
  "sn12.24:2.1": "Then he went to the monastery for the wanderers of other religions and exchanged greetings with the wanderers there. ",
  "sn12.24:2.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side. The wanderers said to him: ",
  "sn12.24:3.1": "“Reverend Sāriputta, there are ascetics and brahmins who teach the efficacy of deeds. Some of them assert that suffering is made by oneself. ",
  "sn12.24:3.2": "Some of them assert that suffering is made by another. ",
  "sn12.24:3.3": "Some of them assert that suffering is made by both oneself and another. ",
  "sn12.24:3.4": "Some of them assert that suffering arises anomalously, not made by oneself or another. ",
  "sn12.24:3.5": "What does the ascetic Gotama say about this? How does he explain it? ",
  "sn12.24:3.6": "How should we answer so as to repeat what the ascetic Gotama has said, and not misrepresent him with an untruth? How should we explain in line with his teaching, with no legitimate 